@startuml
title OpenIM - Message Send Sequence (3.8.3-patch)

autonumber

actor "Client (SDK)" as C
participant "openim-msggateway\n(LongConn/WS)" as GW
participant "openim-rpc-auth\n(gRPC)" as Auth
queue "Kafka" as Kafka
participant "openim-msgtransfer" as Xfer
participant "openim-rpc-msg\n(gRPC)" as Msg
participant "openim-rpc-conversation\n(gRPC)" as Conv
database "Redis" as Redis
database "MongoDB" as Mongo
participant "openim-push" as Push

C -> GW : SendMessage (WS/LongConn)
GW -> Auth : Verify token/session
Auth --> GW : OK (identity)

GW -> Kafka : Publish message event\n(persist/fanout)
Kafka -> Xfer : Deliver message event (consumer)

Xfer -> Msg : Store message / assign seq / indexes
Msg -> Mongo : Persist message / offline records
Mongo --> Msg : OK
Msg -> Redis : Update latest seq / cache
Redis --> Msg : OK
Msg --> Xfer : Stored + seq info

Xfer -> Conv : Update conversation state\n(unread, lastMsg, etc.)
Conv -> Mongo : Persist conversation changes
Mongo --> Conv : OK
Conv --> Xfer : OK

Xfer -> Kafka : Publish push event\n(topic: msgToPush)
Kafka -> Push : Deliver push event (consumer)
Push -> Redis : Lookup online/device/push config
Redis --> Push : Device/setting info
Push --> C : Push notification (APNs/FCM/vendor)

@enduml